1. Sustained high fever, weakness, abdominal pain, loss of appetite, constipation, headache
: Typhoid

Bernoulli gave only 0.01% probability for Typhoid.
Whereas, the ensembles gave 30.44% for Typhoid, the highest probability.


2. High fever, severe joint pain, rash, pain behind the eyes, fatigue, nausea
: Dengue

The ensembles heavily favoured Dengue with 81.18% and gave rest of the diseases 1%/2% only.
KNN had given 100% to Impetigo and Bernoulli had given only 21% to Dengue.

3. Yellowing of skin, yellowing of eyes, dark urine, fatigue, loss of appetite, nausea
: Jaundice

The ensemble has given 71.49% to Hepatitis D and 23.36% to Hepatitis C.
KNN and Bernoulli also had favoured Hepatitis D and other liver related diseases a lot.
This is not an algorithm failure as Jaundice is not a separate disease in itself but is a symptom of Hepatitis.
So, this is a flaw in symptoms labeling in the dataset and the algorithms are not wrong for picking Hepatitis.

4. Excessive thirst, frequent urination, fatigue, blurred vision, unexplained weight loss, slow-healing wounds
: Diabetes

The ensembles gave 59.36% to Diabetes. KNN and Bernoulli also had strongly
favoured Diabetes.

5. Throbbing headache, sensitivity to light, nausea, visual disturbances, dizziness
: Migraine

The ensembles gave Hypertension as 43.63% and Migraine as 28.00%.
In individual algorithms, all of them had favoured Hypertension the most.
Migraine and Hypertension are related very closely so it is not far-fetched.
This is exactly where the probability ranking becomes useful.
[MEDICAL AMBIGUITY]

6. Cough with phlegm, chest pain, fever, breathlessness, fatigue, rapid breathing
: Pneumonia

The individual algorithms had strongly favored Bronchial Asthma.
The ensembles gave:
Bronchial Asthma :  30.83%
Heart attack :  27.49%
Pneumonia :  26.42%

This is again a data problem where the symptoms of Bronchial Asthma and Pneumonia are encoded similarly.
Both the ensembles AND individual algorithms pointing to Bronchial Asthma is not a algorithm fault.
[MEDICAL AMBIGUITY]

7.Itchy red rash, fluid-filled blisters, fever, fatigue, loss of appetite
: Chicken Pox

Another miss due to [MEDICAL AMBIGUITY].
fluid-filled blisters didn't get collapsed into rash but it did into "blisters" so Gemini symptom extraction isn't at fault either.
This is just another case of symptom overlap as blisters belongs to both chicken pox and Impetigo.

8. Burning urination, frequent urge to urinate, cloudy urine, lower abdominal pain, mild fever
: Urinary Tract Infection

The ensembles gave 76.07% to Urinary Tract infection whereas the individuals were also strongly suggesting Urinary Tract Infection.
This shows how well the algorithms work if the symptoms are hyper specific.

9. Heartburn, acid regurgitation, chest discomfort, bloating, difficulty swallowing
: GERD (Acid Reflux)

50.25% to GERD by the ensembles and also by the individuals. Just shows how important the hyper specific symptoms are.

10. Joint pain, joint stiffness (worse in morning), swelling in joints, reduced range of motion, fatigue
: Arthritis

Individuals had given Arthritis due to the specificness of the symptoms and ensembles have given Arthritis a probability of 71.20% and osteoarthritis 11.28%.

11. Wheezing, shortness of breath, chest tightness, coughing, difficulty breathing at night
: Bronchial Asthma

Bronchial Asthma has the least probability whereas Heart attack has 63.75%.
This is another case of [MEDICAL AMBIGUITY] that has more misleading impact as the actual disease is assigned the least possibility whereas the totally unrelated disease is given the biggest probability.

